  "_style": "Standard Kinyarwanda, warm, simple and natural, never flowery or cheesy, never a word-for-word calque of English. Address the user as “wowe” with singular forms (urashobora, yawe, wowe); address the two of them together with “mwe/mwembi” and second-person plural forms (mushobora, yanyu, imperatives in -e such as “Mutere hamwe”); when the user speaks to the partner (messages, letters) write in first person “njye/twe” (ndagutekereza, igiti cyacu). The partner is always “umukunzi wawe” (never umugabo/umugore/fiyanse/umusore/inkumi); Kinyarwanda pronouns and verb prefixes are gender-neutral (we, a-), so keep sentences neutral and never add gendered nouns. A partner's name placeholder (%@) is never declined, contracted or given a prefix/suffix (no “n'%@”, “cya%@”, “kwa%@” glued forms, no class prefix attached): rephrase so it stands alone, e.g. “%@ yateye imbuto” as subject, “byavuye kuri %@”, “hamwe na %@” (write “na” in full, never elide before a placeholder), or use “umukunzi wawe” instead. Use curly quotes “ ” (inner ‘ ’), the single-character ellipsis …, the straight apostrophe ' for normal elision (y'umunsi, n'umukunzi wawe, cy'urukundo), no space before : ; ? !, and keep “ · ”, emoji, \\n and every placeholder exactly as in the source. Numbers: period for thousands, comma for decimals (1.250,5); dates day–month–year with Kinyarwanda month names in lowercase inside sentences (14 Ugushyingo 2026: Mutarama, Gashyantare, Werurwe, Mata, Gicurasi, Kamena, Nyakanga, Kanama, Nzeri, Ukwakira, Ugushyingo, Ukuboza) and let system formatters do the work; 24-hour clock unless the source formats it. Buttons and actions are short singular imperatives (Bika, Ohereza ibaruwa, Ongera ugerageze), no “Mwihangane/Nyamuneka” on buttons; titles, tabs, chips and buttons use sentence case (capital on the first word only) except proper nouns, Coupley, Premium and AI. Latin script only. Plural categories are [\"other\"]: one form for every number, so build sentences where the noun agrees naturally with any count (“iminsi %lld”, “ibiti %lld”, “inzibutso %lld”) and never add a separate singular variant. Keep “Coupley”, “Premium”, “AI” and “CoupleSync” untranslated.",
